<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Sending</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 15)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast sending &lt;item&gt; &lt;person&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>cast sending sword Gandalf
</pre>
<p>The caster raises an item from their inventory and utters 'Selaz', a 
small swirling disk of grey opens above them, and the item rises into it 
and vanishes, to fall from a rift at the feet of the person you named, 
anywhere in the world. They need not be a player: it works for monsters 
too. It lands on the floor beside them, not in their hands.
</p><p>Beware: if the casting only just succeeds, the rift turns a violent red 
and explodes, and the item is lost forever.
</p><p>You can't send a container or a boat, and some places stop the spell: 
you can't send from them, or to someone in them. You must be standing. It 
is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
